DOS_INT21_HANDLER:
        ; INT 21h dispatch entry — branches on AH
        ; DOS_INT21_HANDLER — the entry hooked into IVT[21h] during boot.
        ;
        ; Argument-marshaling pattern used by every DOS_FN_<AH>_* handler in
        ; this binary: the handler is called by DOS_INT21_TABLE_DISPATCH via
        ; `call word [cs:bp+DOS_INT21_FN_TABLE]` with ES:BX pointing at the
        ; saved-register block in DOS_INT21_HANDLER's stack frame. So a handler
        ; body that does:
        ;
        ; les bx, [bp+4]
        ; mov ax, [es:bx+0Eh]   ; saved DS
        ; mov dx, [es:bx+6]     ; saved DX
        ; mov al, [es:bx]       ; saved AX low (function code AL)
        ; ...
        ;
        ; is reading the user's INT 21h registers, not an FCB. The layout matches
        ; the push order in DOS_INT21_HANDLER:
        ; +00 AX, +02 BX, +04 CX, +06 DX, +08 SI, +0A DI,
        ; +0C BP, +0E DS, +10 ES.
        ; Read worker-named labels accordingly: when a handler treats `[bp+4]` as
