DOS_FN_0E_SELECT_DISK:
        ; INT 21h AH=0Eh handler (select disk)
        ; Standard MS-DOS AH=0Eh "Select Default Drive". Sets the current drive
        ; to DL (0=A:, 1=B:, ...). Returns the total drive count in AL.
        ;
        ; Body:
        ; - RESOLVE_DRIVE_MAPPING(DL): walks the DPB chain for substitutions
        ; and returns the physical drive. CF=set if drive is invalid.
        ; - If valid and not redir-flagged (bit 13 of returned AX), store DL
        ; at [2E4h] (current-drive cell). Otherwise fall through without
        ; updating — the existing default stays.
        ; - SET_DEFAULT_DRIVE_TAIL writes the drive count from [1CCh] into
        ; caller's AL (via `les di, [bp+2]; mov [es:di], al`).
